            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the discharge of your 78-year-old male patient, who was admitted on 20/04/2020 following confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection (PCR-positive). On admission, he presented with fever, progressive dyspnoea, and hypoxaemia. Chest X-ray and CT confirmed bilateral viral pneumonia. He required supplemental oxygen therapy and was monitored closely in our respiratory unit. Treatment included dexamethasone, prophylactic low-molecular-weight heparin, and supportive care. No mechanical ventilation was necessary. Inflammatory markers initially elevated (CRP, ferritin, D-dimer) showed a reassuring downward trend prior to discharge. The patient is discharged on 04/05/2020 in recovering condition with oral prednisolone taper and anticoagulation. Please arrange follow-up spirometry and chest imaging in 6–8 weeks. Should you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.</div>"
            },
